------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ElectricSQL — @electric-sql/pglite, package `pglite-sync`
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The read-path sync engine began as a copy of ElectricSQL's `@electric-sql/pglite`
monorepo, package `packages/pglite-sync`:

  Source:  https://github.com/electric-sql/pglite/tree/main/packages/pglite-sync
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Copyright (c) ElectricSQL and contributors

These files derive from it, and each carries a header saying so:

  - src/sync/apply.ts
  - src/sync/subscription-state.ts
  - src/sync/types.ts
  - src/circuits/sync-engine.ts

Their compiled form ships in `dist/`.

Changes: the engine reads each shape from a durable stream rather than Electric's
shape API (ADR-0055); commits each consistency group atomically through a
single-flight commit queue that holds a failed batch instead of dropping it
(ADR-0009); applies through an apply ladder chosen from the registry's column types,
folding each batch to one operation per primary key (ADR-0014); serializes COPY in
Postgres' TEXT format; keeps its metadata in its own `pgxsinkit` schema; and builds
its statements with Drizzle (ADR-0028). The Apache-2.0 terms are permanent. A copy of
the Apache License 2.0 ships with this package in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 (from
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt).

